# CSS Units — rem vs px

Baseline: `html { font-size: 100%; }` in `Styles/Shared/_tokens.css` (16px).

## Use rem (via tokens)

**Font sizes** — always `--text-*`:

```css
.dash-item { font-size: var(--text-md); }
```

**Spacing** — padding, margin, gap — always rem via `--space-*`:

```css
.dash-item { padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-lg); }
.dash-sidebar-inner { padding: var(--space-lg); }
.list-toolbar { gap: var(--space-sm); }
```

| Token | rem | px @ 16px |
|-------|-----|-----------|
| `--space-xs` | 0.25rem | 4 |
| `--space-sm` | 0.5rem | 8 |
| `--space-md` | 0.75rem | 12 |
| `--space-lg` | 1rem | 16 |
| `--space-xl` | 1.5rem | 24 |
| `--space-2xl` | 2rem | 32 |
| `--space-1_5` | 0.375rem | 6 |
| `--space-2_5` | 0.625rem | 10 |
| `--space-3_5` | 0.875rem | 14 |
| `--space-4_5` | 1.125rem | 18 |
| `--space-5` | 1.25rem | 20 |
| `--space-3xl` | 3rem | 48 |
| `--space-section` | 7.5rem | 120 |
| `--control-h` | 2.25rem | 36 |
| `--control-h-lg` | 2.875rem | 46 |

Add new steps to `_tokens.css` before inventing one-off rem values.

## px allowed (small / non-layout)

Use **px only** for properties that should **not** scale with user font settings:

- `border-width` (e.g. `1px`)
- `border-radius` (dashboard: `0`; vitrine CTAs: `2px` max per design system)
- `box-shadow` offsets and blur
- `outline-width` / small `outline-offset`
- Fixed **shell** dimensions: `--sidebar-w`, `--topbar-h`, `--footer-h`

```css
/* OK */
border: 1px solid var(--line);
box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
border-radius: 0;
width: var(--sidebar-w); /* 280px token */
```

## Do not use px for

- `font-size`
- `padding`, `margin`, `gap` on UI components
- `min-height` / `min-width` of buttons, inputs, nav items (use rem)

## Other exceptions

- **Vitrine display type**: `clamp()` with rem/vw for hero headlines
- **Raw rem**: only if no `--text-*` / `--space-*` token exists yet — then add the token

## Do not

- Write `padding: 12px`, `margin: 8px`, or `font-size: 14px` in new CSS
- Duplicate scales in page files — use `_tokens.css` via `app.css`
